{"results":[{"url":"https://thehill.com/homenews/media/4953034-ny-post-endorses-trump/","final_url":"https://thehill.com/homenews/media/4953034-ny-post-endorses-trump/","title":"NY Post endorses Trump after previous criticisms","description":"The New York Post is endorsing former President Trump for president, arguing his record in the White House matters more than his tendency to be “ridiculously hyperbolic.” Writing that T…","language":"en","text":"Media\n\n# NY Post endorses Trump after previous criticisms\n\nby Dominick Mastrangelo - 10/25/24 10:09 AM ET\n\nby Dominick Mastrangelo - 10/25/24 10:09 AM ET\n\nAlex Brandon, Associated Press\n\nRepublican presidential nominee former President Trump dances at a campaign rally at Greensboro Coliseum, Oct. 22, 2024, in Greensboro, N.C.\n\n\n\nThe New York Post is endorsing former President Trump for president, arguing his record in the White House matters more than his tendency to be “ridiculously hyperbolic.”\n\nWriting that Trump “exhibits the same strength and vigor as he did in 2016,” the Post’s editorial board said Trump and Harris “want to take us down very different roads — making the choice stark and simple, but vital.”\n\n“Donald Trump is the right choice,” the Rupert Murdoch-owned newspaper wrote.\n\nThe Post’s endorsement comes after previous criticisms the outlet’s editorial board has hurled at Trump over his managing of the COVID-19 pandemic and actions in the lead-up to the Jan. 6, 2021, attack on the U.S. Capitol by his supporters.\n\nCNN media critic Brian Stelter noted Friday that in in 2022, the Post said Trump had “proven himself unworthy to be this country’s chief executive again.”\n\nThe newspaper has changed its tune less than two weeks out from election day.\n\n“His opponents focus on how Trump’s administration was marked by a relentless soap opera of high drama and chaos — much of which they fueled. And yes, many find him offensive — and we say fair enough: He can be ridiculously hyperbolic,” the Post wrote in its endorsement.\n\n“But before COVID wreaked havoc across the globe, Trump’s first-term results were paychecks that grew markedly faster than inflation, the lowest unemployment in 50 years, a secure border and peace overseas.”\n\nTrump has feuded with Murdoch and a number of the conservative media outlets he owns for months, most notably attacking the Post over its glowing coverage of Florida Gov. Ron DeSantis (R) during the GOP presidential primary.\n\nBut Friday morning, Trump shared the newspaper’s cover story on his Truth Social website, showing a photo of him raising his fist for a crowd in Pennsylvania after being shot in an assassination attempt earlier this year.\n\n“I LOVE THE NEW YORK POST,” he wrote.\n\nAdd as preferred source on Google\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\n\n\n\n## More Media News\n\n## See All\n\nCampaign\n\nby Tara Suter \n\n\n11 hours ago\n\nCampaign \n\n / \n\n11 hours ago\n\nCampaign\n\nby Tara Suter \n\n\n12 hours ago\n\nCampaign \n\n / \n\n12 hours ago\n\nMedia\n\nby Tara Suter \n\n\n15 hours ago\n\nMedia \n\n / \n\n15 hours ago\n\nMedia\n\nby Dominick Mastrangelo \n\n\n15 hours ago\n\nMedia \n\n / \n\n15 hours ago\n\nSee All\n\n## Video/Hill.TV\n\nTHE HILL TV\n\nRising: November 5, 2026\n\nby TheHill.com \n\n\n11/05/26 12:42 PM ET\n\nTHE HILL TV \n\n / \n\n14 hours ago\n\nTHE HILL TV\n\nRising: November 4, 2026\n\nby TheHill.com \n\n\n1 day ago\n\nTHE HILL TV \n\n / \n\n2 days ago\n\nTHE HILL TV\n\nRising: November 3, 2026\n\nby TheHill.com \n\n\n2 days ago\n\nTHE HILL TV \n\n / \n\n3 days ago\n\nSee all Hill.TV \n\n\nSee all Video\n\n## Top Stories\n\n## See All\n\nDefense\n\nby Filip Timotija and Julia Manchester \n\n\n8 hours ago\n\nDefense \n\n / \n\n8 hours ago\n\nSee All","author":"Dominick Mastrangelo","published_date":"2024-10-25T14:09:56+00:00","latency_ms":1889.2902819989104,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}